Seed-ladder audit of the order-58 chain at r = 29
Z(29) = 8281;  a counterexample has cr(G) <= 8280

The rungs, weakest first, with sources in verify_range.py:
   counting only, cr(K_13) >= 217
   McQuillan-Pan-Richter JCTB 2015, cr(K_13) >= 219
   Abrego et al. EuroCG 2015, cr(K_13) >= 223
   Aichholzer CCCG 2021, cr(K_13) = 225

RUNG: counting only, cr(K_13) >= 217     cr(K_27) >= 5357, cr(K_28) >= 6250
   piece 1, m=838: 1 of the |R| rows die by the Gallai cap, 1 by the split bound, 0 by neither
   piece 1, m=839: 2 of the |R| rows die by the Gallai cap, 3 by the split bound, 0 by neither
   piece 1, m=840: 2 of the |R| rows die by the Gallai cap, 5 by the split bound, 0 by neither
   piece 2: split minima [10714, 10714, 10714] against 8281  -> holds
   piece 3: classes with b >= 8 surviving [0, 0, 0]  -> holds
   => order 58 reduces to the three b <= 7 classes: YES

