CONCLUSION
   Every piece of the order-58 chain holds at every rung, so the
   whole reduction needs nothing beyond cr(K_12) = 150 (Guy;
   Pan and Richter, J. Graph Theory 56 (2007) 128-134).  In
   particular it does NOT need the CCCG 2021 value cr(K_13) = 225,
   which is a published but single-author, 1000+ CPU-year result
   that neither Schaefer's DS21 (2026) nor Clancy-Haythorpe-
   Newcombe records.
   Piece 3 required crminus.py to reach this: without it, b = 30
   survived at the weakest rung (8249 at m = 839, 8213 at m = 840).
   Pieces 1 and 2 were already seed-independent; this file is the
   check that establishes it, which had not been done before.

   STILL OPEN: the three classes b = 6 with (51,1) and (50,1,1) and
   b = 7 with (49,1,1), and the three order-57 rows 826, 827, 828.
